{
  "_readme": "These Kimi Code values cross the Go and TypeScript boundary. LeapMux runs `kimi web` and drives its kap-server through REST and one WebSocket. Each event payload repeats its frame type. The Worker stores the payload unchanged. The browser dispatches on those same event types. The events table includes every declared server event, including the server-added event.* family. The origins table identifies who starts a turn. The tools and displayKinds tables identify tools and control displays. The decision and answer tables hold native reply values. The goalModes table holds approval labels. The modes table combines the three native permission modes with LeapMux plan mode. Moonshot AI owns these values except the two reply marks. LeapMux chooses dismiss for the dedicated dismiss route. LeapMux chooses permission_mode for the mode after plan approval. The todoStatuses and turnEndReasons tables hold native task and completion values. The browser owns native output headers and per-line footers in its provider protocol module. The opening event supplies the tool name because native result events contain no name. Per-line footers contain no declared length. The browser shows the reported output_path beside the original preview. It checks native session and agent identity. It checks native turn and call identity also. LeapMux reads no output file.",
